You are judging whether the sr-test CASES of ONE RULE, taken together, are RIGOROUS. A case is a folder
`tests/<case>/` inside the folder of the ONE rule it proves (`.sloprail/<gate|file-guard|context>/<rule>/tests/<case>/`,
or `.sloprail/file-guard/structure.tests/<case>/` for the structure gate), holding a `test.sh` (and usually an
`agent.sh`, and mock judge scripts). sr-test runs `test.sh` against a scripted agent and the real rule engine;
a case proves that the rule actually fires. A rule whose cases pass whatever the rule does is slop: it sits in
the project looking like coverage and checks nothing.

